course: dictionary
lesson: 15155
title: One word, different jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can do more than one job in a sentence. Scissor is a verb when you cut or open and close, and it is also used before another noun. «Sam scissored the card into a neat heart.» Here scissored is an action: Sam cut the card with scissors.
explain: «The footballer scored with a scissor kick.» Scissor comes before kick, so it tells you what kind of kick it was. A scissor kick is a move where the legs open and close like scissors. Look at the word after scissor to find its job.
explain: «The workers rose high on a scissor lift.» A scissor lift is a platform that goes up and down. Scissor is describing the lift, not naming a tool. Ask yourself: is this word doing an action, or is it describing the next word?
fact: Scissor can be a verb: to cut with scissors, or to open and close like scissors.
fact: Scissor used before another noun describes it, as in «scissor blade», «scissor kick» and «scissor lift».
fact: The everyday tool is called «scissors», as in «a pair of scissors».
fact: Verb forms are scissor, scissors, scissored and scissoring: «She is scissoring the paper now.»
fact: In school, carry scissors with the points down so nobody gets hurt.
exercise: «Sam scissored the card into a neat heart.» What does scissored mean? | Folded very small | *Cut with scissors | Coloured in bright red | Glued to a wall
exercise: «Ava did a scissor kick and the ball flew into the net.» In «scissor kick», what job does scissor do? | It is the name of a person | *It describes the kind of kick | It means the ball is round | It means the net is open
exercise: «We need a pair of scissors for the craft lesson.» Find and copy the word that names the tool. | craft | lesson | pair | *scissors
test: «The swimmer's legs scissored open and shut in the kick.» What does scissored mean here? | Stopped suddenly | *Opened and closed like scissors | Sank under the water | Cut in half
test: «The builders went up on a scissor lift.» What is a scissor lift? | A type of shoe | A kind of pair of scissors | A swimming race | *A platform that goes up and down
exam: «The scissor blade was sharp.» In «scissor blade», what kind of blade is it? | A round blade for spinning | A blade made of wood | *A blade linked to scissors | A blade for bread
